{"parentUuid":"237d5875-9b15-4d15-aba4-c6a8301985b5","isSidechain":false,"userType":"external","cwd":"/Users/devin/repos/a2-ai/test-build-processes","sessionId":"7f22a452-0af5-4c0c-be1c-699e971cf878","version":"2.0.22","gitBranch":"main","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"I would now like to set up a separate release pipeline that is similar to the existing release pipeline, but to expand the capabilities to allow for generation of .deb files after the build. I believe this will take a multistage build as we want the binary built on the almalinux container, but the debs to be assembled by go releaser later. Here is a goreleaser we've used from argus, which we use the deb in order to run some additional scripts to give the binary some additional capabilities + install to usr/local/bin. For this repo, do a simple hook, it does not need to be fancy, just something to show we can generate a full deb. version: 2\n\nbefore:\n  hooks:\n    # Ensure all dependencies are available\n    - cargo fetch --locked\n    # Disable wild linker and sccache for CI builds (faster to skip setup than use them)\n    - sh -c 'if [ -f .cargo/config.toml ]; then mv .cargo/config.toml .cargo/config.toml.bak; fi'\n\nbuilds:\n  - id: argus\n    builder: rust\n    binary: argus\n    # Use regular cargo build since we're building natively\n    command: build\n    # This is a workspace project, so we need to specify the package\n    flags:\n      - --release\n      - -p=argus\n    # For cross-compilation to work in CI, run goreleaser on native runners:\n    # - Use ubuntu-latest (x86_64) for x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\n    # - Use ubuntu-24.04-arm64 for aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu\n    # Or run goreleaser separately on each architecture and merge artifacts\n    targets:\n      - x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu\n      - aarch64-unknown-linux-gnu\narchives:\n  - id: argus-archive\n    format_overrides:\n      - goos: linux\n        format: tar.gz\n    name_template: >-\n      {{ .ProjectName }}_\n      {{- .Version }}_\n      {{- .Os }}_\n      {{- .Arch }}\n    files:\n      - README.md\n      - LICENSE*\n      - CLAUDE.md\n\nnfpms:\n  - id: argus-deb\n    package_name: argus\n    vendor: a2-ai\n    homepage: https://github.com/a2-ai/github-ci\n    maintainer: a2-ai Team\n    description: |\n      Argus - eBPF-based file tracer for process I/O monitoring\n      Records file reads/writes for a target process and its descendants\n    license: MIT\n    formats:\n      - deb\n\n    # Install binary to /usr/local/bin\n    bindir: /usr/local/bin\n\n    # Dependencies required for setting capabilities\n    dependencies:\n      - libcap2-bin\n\n    # Set file permissions\n    file_name_template: >-\n      {{ .ProjectName }}_\n      {{- .Version }}_\n      {{- .Arch }}\n\n    # Scripts for installation lifecycle\n    scripts:\n      postinstall: scripts/postinstall.sh\n      preremove: scripts/preremove.sh\n\n    # File metadata\n    contents:\n      - src: scripts/postinstall.sh\n        dst: /usr/share/doc/argus/postinstall.sh\n        type: config\n      - src: scripts/preremove.sh\n        dst: /usr/share/doc/argus/preremove.sh\n        type: config\n\nchecksum:\n  name_template: 'checksums.txt'\n\nsnapshot:\n  version_template: \"{{ incpatch .Version }}-next\"\n\nchangelog:\n  sort: asc\n  filters:\n    exclude:\n      - '^docs:'\n      - '^test:'\n      - '^ci:'\n      - '^chore:'\n      - Merge pull request\n      - Merge branch\n\n# Release configuration (won't be used for snapshot builds)\nrelease:\n  github:\n    owner: a2-ai\n    name: argus \n  draft: true\n  prerelease: auto use this as a SEPARATE release build and pipeline so we can show the different ways to release a simple binary via the existing process, and this would be a separate example"},"uuid":"57e2b214-8f4d-41ce-a237-07123ea8dcb6","timestamp":"2025-10-18T14:18:43.766Z","thinkingMetadata":{"level":"none","disabled":true,"triggers":[]}}
